    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656-a1">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1028" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg1028"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex 1 to dispatch No. 186.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wheelock to Mr. Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Trinidad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 4,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you herewith my
                    letter to the Trinidad Chronicle, containing a brief description of the infamous
                    action of a civil officer of the Venezuelan <pb facs="1129" n="1029"
                        xml:id="pg1029"/> Government, by which I was the sufferer. The proceedings
                    as I have described them are strictly true in every particular, and in no way
                    exaggerated.</p>
                <p>I claim $50,000 as a small compensation for what I have been compelled to endure,
                    and I most earnestly and respectfully request your assistance in enforcing this
                    claim against the Venezuelan Government.</p>
                <p>I am now on my way to New York, and my address will be at 66 Willow street,
                    Brooklyn, N. Y.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN E. WHEELOCK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
